## 2. Architectural Deficits & What Needs to Change

| Feature | Current Implementation | Target Production Architecture |
|---|---|---|
| **API Server** | None (only sender script) | FastAPI `POST /webhooks` returning `202 Accepted` or `201 Created` immediately with job ID |
| **Worker Decoupling** | Synchronous thread loop | Celery worker consuming tasks from Redis queues |
| **Persistence** | Raw psycopg2 with hardcoded SQL | SQLAlchemy / robust connection pool with migrations & schema extension |
| **Schema** | Missing `target_url`, `idempotency_key`, `event_type`, `headers` | Non-destructive schema migration adding required fields + `webhook_deliveries` attempts table |
| **Retry Strategy** | Blocking `time.sleep(2)` | Celery native exponential backoff with jitter and configurable retry limits (`countdown=base * (2 ** retry)`) |
| **Attempt Tracking** | Overwrites `attempts` count only | Detailed audit table (`webhook_deliveries`) recording timestamps, status code, latency (ms), and error trace |
| **Security** | None | HMAC SHA256 signature header (`X-Webhook-Signature`) with shared secret verification |
| **Idempotency** | Duplicate payloads create multiple deliveries | Idempotency keys (`Idempotency-Key` or `event_id`) to deduplicate rapid dispatch requests |
| **Observability** | Console print statements | Python structured logging + modern live dashboard |
| **Configuration** | Hardcoded passwords in source files | Centralized `.env` and `app/config.py` using Pydantic Settings |

